Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
Guard extraction: termination, soundness, completeness \[LongDash] Findings \
(v0)\
\>", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"1eb28169-b252-4a32-862a-05d2599bc36c"],

Cell["\<\
gtpyhop-diagnostics, commit caa3a1b: atoms come straight from the success \
analysis\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"66364a91-55e4-4ec1-a8a5-b285dfdaffe6"],

Cell["\<\
type: findings
topic: diagnostics_guard_cf
date: 2026-11-17
version: v0
prior-version: round 00 (00-findings_guard_control_flow_v0), commit dc3f852
key-metric: necessary literals missed where tests are independent and no \
success return is inside a loop: 0 of every action body of \[LessEqual] 6 \
statements
decision-required: confirm\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"3783c470-900b-499d-a6f5-f24b5a6bdfeb"],

Cell["Headline Result", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ffd7d43c-f741-472a-bd2d-33c6dfb5bbbd"],

Cell["\<\
metric:    bodies where the atoms are not exactly the necessary literals, \
tests independent, no success return inside a loop
value:     0 of 80,443  (caa3a1b)
unit:      action bodies
prior:     not established (round 00 proved soundness only)
direction: down\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"6695e572-e066-4b41-ab7b-30c8bf6dd0ed"],

Cell["\<\
Round 00 proved that dc3f852 never reports an atom that a successful run can \
violate (soundness: no false positives). This round asks the converse, and \
two practical questions around it: does the analysis always finish, does it \
report every precondition it could (completeness: no missed true positives), \
and what does a reported atom guarantee to whoever acts on it. Answering the \
second found a gap: dc3f852 dropped requirements the analysis had proved \
whenever the failing side of an if was not spelled return False. caa3a1b \
closes it by emitting atoms straight from the analysis, and changes no atom \
on the bundled examples or the 436-domain corpus.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7eab5104-c75f-48ca-8cde-fee36224b2fb"],

Cell["Model", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"8aaf2b4d-4bc8-49e3-9db1-c20de358dd6f"],

Cell["\<\
The model is round 00's, unchanged: inert statements ok (return state), bail \
(return False, None, bare return, raise), eff (an effect), if[id, t, A, B] \
and loop[id, A], over tests p, q, r. sem[P, False] is the condition under \
which the action succeeds. an mirrors guards._required_on_success and returns \
{mayOk, R}: whether the block may succeed, and the set R of (if, polarity) \
pairs that every successful path passes. dc3f852 reported R filtered by the \
old per-if reading; caa3a1b reports R itself.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5b77079f-1271-40ad-84ed-277667ba5ab3"],

Cell["\<\
Vocabulary. A literal is one if test with a direction, t or not t. A literal \
is necessary when every successful run satisfies it, i.e. sem \
\[DoubleLongRightArrow] literal. Soundness: every reported literal is \
necessary. Completeness: every necessary literal is reported. A body that can \
never succeed makes every literal vacuously necessary; such atoms say \
nothing, and are counted apart.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"36511fb4-b5dc-4a00-bf6e-aefbbabe5cd9"],

Cell["Results Tables", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"53aab078-b00c-4b29-a5a0-552f231d0b60"],

Cell["R1. Termination and cost", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"3bcff378-b4d5-4768-be53-a42f980f586e"],

Cell["\<\
an recurses only on strictly smaller terms: the rest of a statement list, or \
the branches of an if. Every recursion therefore stops, by structural \
induction, with no fixpoint iteration: a loop is summarised in one step by \
scanning its body for a success return (succIn), never iterated. Each \
statement outside a loop body costs one step, so the analysis is linear in \
the number of statements; the Python code adds one scan of the subtree under \
each loop, with or try, so at most statements \[Times] nesting depth.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4ff03f9d-7d52-4925-bbd2-50e3f1c3b393"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Length", "[", "progs", "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       FractionBox[
        RowBox[{"#1", "[", "\"\<steps\>\"", "]"}], 
        RowBox[{"#1", "[", "\"\<size\>\"", "]"}]], "&"}], ")"}], "/@", 
     "prof"}], "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"AllTrue", "[", 
    RowBox[{"prof", ",", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"#1", "[", "\"\<steps\>\"", "]"}], "\[LessEqual]", 
       RowBox[{"#1", "[", "\"\<size\>\"", "]"}]}], "&"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "}"}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ec348e43-f628-4ae3-bb11-f1197419d36a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"94350", ",", "1", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->\
"2c10e7d1-1e35-424e-9e3e-f4e9b536cfc5"],

Cell["\<\
Bodies checked, the largest ratio of analysis steps to statements, and \
whether every body stays within one step per statement.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"887c8191-3be0-4f83-92c1-924cfe47ce0b"],

Cell["R2. Soundness carries over", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"440f67c6-06a8-40e9-8def-54715b9d28df"],

Cell["\<\
Round 00 R2 proved, by induction on the statement list, that every literal in \
R is necessary and that mayOk = False only for bodies that cannot succeed. \
Its last row covered the filter dc3f852 applied (kept \[SubsetEqual] R); \
caa3a1b keeps all of R, the case kept = R, so the proof applies unchanged. \
Exhaustive re-check: atoms reported by each reading, split into sound and \
informative (the body can succeed), vacuous (it cannot), and unsound.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1832fb35-c4fe-421b-97bd-00f7771d4d18"],

