  "Grid"]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"4558a122-8ed6-4d5d-b34c-daac5316d3fa"],

Cell["Scope: what this does not prove", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"3091316c-7231-4cf3-9023-56526af47e25"],

Cell["\<\
Tests are read on the state the action was called on. A test that reads state \
the action has already changed is outside the model, for soundness and \
completeness alike.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c317b54b-b026-4d42-a18f-9b6c182222e9"],

Cell["\<\
Completeness is relative: to independent tests, to success returns outside \
loops, and to the literals of if tests. Round 00's splitting of each \
requirement into atoms is a separate step with its own precision.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"09c07311-1212-44b8-b45f-d2624bcc4feb"],

Cell["\<\
The bundled and corpus counts are measurements \
(diagnostics_guard_nnf/scripts), listed in the commit message: no atom \
changes between dc3f852 and caa3a1b, recognition 330 of 335 and 5,807 of \
5,885.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4ca6474d-40f9-44f7-b9d1-b5d71eae5ef8"],

