Cell["\<\
Caption: dc3f852 removes every unsound atom (red) and most vacuous ones \
(light grey), and loses informative atoms (dark grey, 17,085 to 13,566) in \
loops and repeated tests. caa3a1b stays sound and reports 54,252 informative \
atoms: most enumerated bodies fail by falling through, which the per-if \
reading of both earlier versions could not see (R4). Real domains spell their \
failures as return False, so there dc3f852 and caa3a1b give the same atoms.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"860cfe1d-07a6-4de0-88a3-a1af6e8bc477"],

Cell["Contradictions & Surprises", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"fc435295-7c5a-40ee-8b81-c65852b2fe7a"],

Cell["\<\
Round 00 attributed every precision loss to loops and repeated tests. That \
was true of the atoms dc3f852 dropped relative to 0.1.1, but both versions \
shared a third, larger miss: the per-if reading never produced an atom for an \
if whose failing side falls through. It shows up only when completeness is \
measured against the success condition rather than against the previous \
version.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"0c9094a1-23fe-41db-9d82-b7ecaf71f095"],

Cell["\<\
Closing it changed nothing measurable in practice: every bundled and corpus \
action already spells its failing side as a return.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e2a50a88-cbc5-4abc-a5ec-a717bcf844ea"],

Cell["Steering Questions", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"772f5c1d-600a-4ffd-ab61-a199539d5e01"],

Cell["\<\
[now] Keep caa3a1b in the same PR as dc3f852? It turns the proof from sound \
into sound and relatively complete, and removes the per-if classifier.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"aca00f9a-bca4-4359-8b54-399b93eab5c5"],

Cell["\<\
[next run] Make the consumer contract explicit to whoever reads \
explain_dead_end (an agent, a person): a false atom is necessary, the list is \
not sufficient, and alternatives are never atoms. A separate change.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b2c9c16d-1489-468a-865d-b6ae2a8fb514"],

Cell["\<\
[next run] A test that reads state the action has already written. Measure \
how often it occurs before deciding whether to model writes.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"16388059-dfad-4e7c-add0-b6b7f5892ca7"],

Cell["References", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"09420c3b-a052-4a96-9ceb-7beee77f88ca"],

Cell["\<\
G. A. Kildall, A unified approach to global program optimization, POPL 1973. \
The dataflow framework: the analysis is a backward must-analysis, meet = \
intersection.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4e05666b-1eb0-4ed5-973e-f658994dbb22"],

Cell["\<\
T. Lengauer, R. E. Tarjan, A fast algorithm for finding dominators in a \
flowgraph, ACM TOPLAS 1(1), 1979. R is the set of branch edges that dominate \
every success return.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"a24b70ca-2198-44cd-9042-f14af1b8fc83"],

Cell["\<\
K. D. Cooper, T. J. Harvey, K. Kennedy, A simple, fast dominance algorithm, \
Software: Practice and Experience, 2001. The iterative form, which a \
control-flow-graph version would use to recover R4's loop literals.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"dc90cee5-0f53-4c5c-a088-29b252d7ae5c"],

Cell["\<\
P. Cousot, R. Cousot, M. F\[ADoubleDot]hndrich, F. Logozzo, Automatic \
inference of necessary preconditions, VMCAI 2013, LNCS 7737. The same goal: \
conditions whose violation guarantees failure.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"820adaf9-ef2b-447b-97bf-4171c8137953"],

Cell["\<\
M. Das, S. Lerner, M. Seigle, ESP: path-sensitive program verification in \
polynomial time, PLDI 2002. A route to R4's repeated-test literals.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"8d33d1c6-d20a-44ef-8236-69c28cdc4ccb"],

Cell["Pointers", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"da2d165c-1bb2-4d60-a7eb-52dbe3943d03"],

Cell["\<\
Commits dc3f852 (sound), caa3a1b (complete), on top of round 00 of \
diagnostics_guard_nnf\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f3924d8f-b624-486a-8a15-05f684a2a063"],

Cell["\<\
tools/diagnostics_guard_check.py: 16 cases, including the executed soundness \
and completeness property cases\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"2616525b-f83c-4e47-bc1b-d1e6c33d4398"],

Cell["\<\
Round 00 of this topic: 00-findings_guard_control_flow_v0, whose build pins \
dc3f852\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"7f8c651f-8e8b-4728-8936-b1e3c3aa44b7"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Appendix: definitions (initialization cells)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1394f46c-ef0c-405c-8462-e0e218179fa1"],

Cell["\<\
Round 00's model (sem, an, oldReq, newReq, the enumeration), with an counting \
its steps in $steps. cur is the caa3a1b reading, fresh gives every if its own \
test, exact the literals the success condition then implies, profile one \
truth table per program. U, ex and ifRule are the finite universe of R3.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9620a6f5-dc79-4e81-87f8-67f58db5d709"],

